float popTime = stack.getPopTime() - deltaTracker.getGameTimeDeltaPartialTick(false);
if (popTime > 0) {
   float f = 1.0F + popTime / 5.0F;          // scale = 1 + popTime/5
   pose.pushMatrix();
   pose.translate(x + 8, y + 12);
   pose.scale(1.0F / f, (f + 1.0F) / 2.0F);
   pose.translate(-(x + 8), -(y + 12));
}
extractor.item(player, stack, x, y, zOffset);
...
extractor.itemDecorations(font, stack, x, y);
```
So the vanilla pop: popTime starts at 5 (item pop time set to 5 ticks on selection change? Actually ItemStack.getPopTime() for LocalPlayer is decremented each tick; `Player.getInventory().selected` change triggers `itemstack.setPopTime(5)`). Scale x = 1/f, y = (f+1)/2 where f = 1 + pop/5 → at pop=5: f=2 → scaleX=0.5, scaleY=1.5 — that's the classic squash/stretch. Pivot at (x+8, y+12) i.e. item center-x, bottom-y. Duration 5 ticks (250 ms), centered at (x+8, y+12).

